        "footnotes": [
          "(1) The pipefitter or boilermaker should be alert to flange distortion and bolting elongation.",
          "(2) For flange materials not listed (excluding cast iron), initial bolt stress should be equal to 30,000 psi times the ratio of the pressure rating at 100°F to the pressure rating for carbon steel at 100°F.",
          "(3) For conversion of bolting stress to torque, see Figure 600-6.",
          "(4) ASME/ANSI B16.5 includes cast or forged steel flanges from preceding standard ASA-B16.e.",
          "(5) For Class 150 flanges of Types 304, 304L, or 316L stainless steel: the flange should be carefully observed for evidence of distortion.",
          "(6) If bolting is other than A193, engineering review is recommended unless suitable loadings are known from previous experience.",
          "(7) If leaks develop, these stresses should be increased by up to 1/3 (without engineering review) if there is not evidence of flange distortion.",
          "(8) Some Class 150 piping classifications permit mild steel bolts for flange diameters through 16\" with up to 1\" bolts with minimum yield strength of 30,000 psi.",
          "(9) Cast iron flanges require full face gaskets and mild steel bolts."
        ],
